With a project as large as SE Linux there will always be things that aren't 
being developed as much as they could be, especially when there's only about 
half a dozen people working on it.

Also the NSA people are not working on any commercial aspects of the 
technology, so any work that is focussed directly on commercial aspects is 
probably something that no-one else is doing much on.

> day to learn it (5 days a week) what would you suggest and how would you
> suggest mastering that aspect?

I could list 100 things, and I have listed many things on the list in the 
past, check the archives.

In general the thing to do is to read the list and look for a message from one 
of the people doing development saying "we should probably work on X but I 
haven't got the time", which is an invitation to you to step in and start 
doing something.

